error[dli::syntax::curly-quote]: that is a curly quote — write labels with straight quotes, like "Camelot".
  --> line 1:12
  |
1 | place weir “The Weir” proposed
  |            ^ curly quote
  |
  = what: a curly (smart) quote appears where a label's straight-quoted text belongs — the artifact an editor leaves when it auto-replaces quotes
  = fix:  replace the curly quote with a straight `"`
  = rule: there is one way to write a label — straight quotes — so the canonical surface never turns on a character an editor might substitute unseen  (koan 7 — one way to write it; 01-syntax.md §1)
